  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.42",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(a) If X is a smooth, closed, simply connected 4-manifold $withb_{2}(X) \\geq$ 2, are all knots slice in X?\n\n(b) In particular, are all knots slice in $\\mathbb{CP}^{2}\\#\\overline{\\mathbb{CP}}{}^{2}$? In the K3 surface?\n\n(c) Can the set of slice knots detect exotic smooth structures? That is, do there exist homeomorphic 4-manifolds X and $X^{1}$ and a knot $K \\subset S^{3}$ that is slice in X but not in $X^{1}$?",
